Pace frontend audio like a host audio device

The libretro sink pushed the renderer's output straight into a queue, as
if it were stereo, and never counted its buffers, so nothing paced the
emulated renderer. retro_run then handed the frontend whatever fit in
one frame of that and dropped the rest, which sounded broken.

Let the primary stream queue its buffers as host streams do, with their
downmix and volume, and have retro_run take one frame per call through
ProcessAudioOutAndRender, like a device callback. The renderer then runs
only a few buffers ahead of the frontend. As nothing takes audio after
the last retro_run, detach the streams before shutting down.

